Dynamic training does not change the inference architecture, so its inference speed is effectively identical to that of static training.
Its overhead is therefore concentrated in the training phase, where temporal unrolling increases both wall-clock time and memory usage.
Since this behavior is expected and not central to our main contribution, we report it only as a compact ratio-based cost comparison.

